# core.autocrlf=true is set globally on this machine, which rewrites the WORKING
# COPY to CRLF on checkout. Deployment copies files straight from the working copy
# into ~/.claude/, so without this the deployed files drift to CRLF — and checks.sh
# is a bash script: CRLF makes it die with `$'\r': command not found`.
# Everything here stays LF on disk, not just in git.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
